headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{idToken}}
}

docs {
  # Shuttle Connect API

  Every successful response is wrapped by `ResponseTransformInterceptor`:

  ```json
  { "success": true, "data": { ... } }
  ```

  Every error is shaped by `GlobalExceptionFilter`:

  ```json
  { "success": false, "error": { "code": "...", "statusCode": 400, "message": "..." } }
  ```

  So assertions read `res.body.data.*` on success and `res.body.error.code` on failure.

  ## Running the flow

  Requests are sequenced so `bru run` executes them in dependency order:
  Courts -> Sessions -> Requests. Each create step writes its id into an
  environment variable (`courtId`, `sessionId`) for the next one to use.
}
